  "notes": "BinDawood Holding Company (a Saudi Joint Stock Company, ticker 4161) audited consolidated financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2025 with FY2024 comparatives, from the full audited PDF in the 'Annual / 2025' cell of the Saudi Exchange company-profile 'Financial Statements' tab (Resources/fsPdf/1821_0_2026-03-18...). Auditor KPMG. All five primary statements (printed pages 5-12) are scanned images in the filed PDF (transcribed from page renders at 2.5x); the notes are digital text. Amounts are in full Saudi Riyals (scale 1). Board of Directors approved the statements on 20 Ramadan 1447H / 9 March 2026 (used as filed_at). income_taxes_and_zakat is the single reported 'Zakat and tax expense'. operating_income is the reported 'Operating profit' (after other operating income of SAR 5.9m); other_operating_revenue carries that 'Other operating income' line and other_income is the separate 'Other income' below operating profit. share_of_profit_associates is 'Share of loss from equity-accounted investment' (a SAR 1.0m loss in 2025; nil 2024). intangible_assets is the combined 'Intangible assets and goodwill' line (the SAR 336m step-up vs 2024 is from acquisitions during the year). long_term_investments is 'Investment at fair value through other comprehensive income'; investments_associates is 'Equity-accounted investment' (new in 2025). other_reserves combines the foreign currency translation reserve, the employees' share-based-payments reserve and 'Other reserves'; treasury_shares is the 'Treasury shares reserve'. long_term_debt / current_debt are the non-current / current 'Bank borrowings' (both new in 2025 - the group took on bank debt to fund acquisitions); bonds_sukuk is the 'Compulsory convertible debentures'; IFRS 16 lease liabilities are mapped separately. related_party_payables is 'Due to related parties'; contract_liabilities is 'Unearned income and other payable'. depreciation_amortization sums depreciation on property and equipment, depreciation on right-of-use assets and amortisation of intangible assets from the cash-flow statement. capex is 'Acquisition of property and equipment'. interest_paid sums 'Finance cost paid on lease liabilities' and 'Interest expense on bank borrowing'. zakat_paid is 'Zakat and tax paid'. The cash-flow statement reconciles with a separate 'Effect of movements in exchange rates on cash held' line. Statement page references are the printed page numbers: financial position 5-6, profit or loss and OCI 7-8, changes in equity 9-10, cash flows 11-12.",
